# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-chakra/blob/d0d45ae1d26ca1b87034e67180fac07ce9642fd9/solidity/settlement/contracts/ChakraSettlement.sol#L158-L244


# Vulnerability details

## Impact

The `receive_cross_chain_msg` function in the `ChakraSettlement` contract lacks proper access control for validators. An attacker can front-run the validator's call with their valid signatures and call `receive_cross_chain_msg` with his own address to steal tokens.

*Note that the same issue persists in the Cairo code.*

## Vulnerability Details
Chakra audit details
Total Prize Pool: $60,000 in USDT
HM awards: $43,200 in USDT
QA awards: $1,800 in USDT
Judge awards: $4,500 in USDT
To receive a cross-chain message, a validator calls `receive_cross_chain_msg` function with enough valid signatures (>= `required_validators`):
[https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-chakra/blob/d0d45ae1d26ca1b87034e67180fac07ce9642fd9/solidity/settlement/contracts/ChakraSettlement.sol#L158-L244](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-chakra/blob/d0d45ae1d26ca1b87034e67180fac07ce9642fd9/solidity/settlement/contracts/ChakraSettlement.sol#L158-L244)

```js
function receive_cross_chain_msg(
    uint256,
