## Impact
These four Cairo functions accept signatures to validate requests that result in critical actions, including minting, burning, locking, and unlocking tokens. All of these functions use the same `check_chakra_signatures` function to validate signatures, making them all vulnerable. A single Chakra validator can submit their signature `required_validators_num` times in a row, bypassing the requirement that `required_validators` distinct validator signatures are needed to execute these functions.

