## Vulnerability details
In `'ChakraSettlementHandler::cross_chain_erc20_settlement'`, users can send cross chain transactions to  others chains, by specifying which token to use in the destination chain in the field `'to_token'`.

The problem is that the ChakraSettlementHandler and the ChakraSettlement do not check if the token that has been locked by the user and the token unlocked in the destination chain is the same.

## Impact
Malicious users could call `'ChakraSettlementHandler::cross_chain_erc20_settlement'` in a HandlerSettlement where the price of the token is lower that the token unlocked on the destination chain. 

Let's take as example LINK and WETH, imaging that LINK is worth 10 dollars and WETH is worth 2000 dollars per token. 

User could lock 100 LINK on the source chain, locking a total value of 1000 dollars and unlock 100 WETH on the destination chain, unlocking a total value of 200.000 dollars, draining a part of the funds in the handler contract in the destination chain.

