## Vulnerability details
When users perform cross chain transactions using a `ChakraSettlementHandler` with mode `LockMint`, the funds locked in the handler on the source chain cannot be withdrawn or unlocked. In the contract there is not the logic to manage those assets and for this reason they will result as unusable and if they are ERC20 tokens that do not supports the `ChakraToken` implementation, those can't be neither burned. 

En fact, differently from the `MintBurn` mode when a burn on the callback is performed, in the mode `LockMint` this will not happen. 

The funds cannot be withdrawn because there is not a logic for that, neither the handler owner can, they can't also be unlocked since the mode is `LockMint` and when 
`'ChakraSettlementHandler::receive_cross_chain_msg'` is triggered, the contract will mint others tokens to the users and it can't unlock the actual tokens in the contract also if they are available. 

## Impact
If the funds get locked in an handler with MintLock mode, no one will be able to withdraw and unlock those funds. The liquidity created in that handler will be no utilizable. 

