## Vulnerability details
In `ChakraSettlementHandler::cross_chain_erc20_settlement` there is not any input validation for the fields `to_chain`, `to_handler` and `to_token`. 

Differently from the `Cairo` codebase, in the `Solidity` contracts there is not the validation and the assurance that these input are valid.

## Impact
This vulnerability may have a big impact on the cross chain transaction. Users, by mistake could pass a bad name for `to_chain` or / and pass a bad value for `to_handler` or / and pass a bad value for `to_token`. 

This is a problem because since there is not any input validation, the cross chain transaction on the chain A won't fail, but then, the validators may have several problem to send the cross chain transaction on the destination chain (chain B). 
An user could lock his funds on chain A but he could not receive nothing on the chain B, and so, he will lose all the funds that he locked in the handler contract on chain A. 

This problem is also amplified by the fact that there is not he logic to withdraw the locked funds in the contract.

