# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The `nonce_manager` storage variable can easily be manipulated by calling `ChakraSettlement::send_cross_chain_msg` [here](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-chakra/blob/d0d45ae1d26ca1b87034e67180fac07ce9642fd9/solidity/settlement/contracts/ChakraSettlement.sol#L118)

The impact is `txid` across contracts will not match and `ChakraSettlement::receive_cross_chain_callback` will always revert.

## Proof of Concept
Steps to attack:
1. Call `ChakraSettlement::send_cross_chain_msg` [here](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-chakra/blob/d0d45ae1d26ca1b87034e67180fac07ce9642fd9/solidity/settlement/contracts/ChakraSettlement.sol#L111) with arbitrary data. There are no checks for valid data and it will most likely not be processed on the destination chain. However, the important thing is the `nonce_manager` for any desired address can/will be incremented.

2. Now a user whose nonce was manipulated will normally interact with the protocol through the `ChakraSettlementHandler::cross_chain_erc20_settlement` to transfer ERC20 tokens cross-chain. In the function call there is external call to the `ChakraSettlement` contract [here](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-chakra/blob/d0d45ae1d26ca1b87034e67180fac07ce9642fd9/solidity/handler/contracts/ChakraSettlementHandler.sol#L203). This will generate the `txid` in the settlement contract which would be the same as in the handler if the nonce for the user was the same. However, the `txid` will be different.

3. In `ChakraSettlement::receive_cross_chain_callback` the `txid` sent [here](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-chakra/blob/d0d45ae1d26ca1b87034e67180fac07ce9642fd9/solidity/settlement/contracts/ChakraSettlement.sol#L318) will be incorrect

4. `ChakraSettlementHandler::receive_cross_chain_callback` will receive the incorrect `txid` and will always revert [here](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-chakra/blob/d0d45ae1d26ca1b87034e67180fac07ce9642fd9/solidity/settlement/contracts/ChakraSettlement.sol#L313)

