# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Anyone can destroy the `ChakraSettlement.sol` contract by upgrading it to a malicious contract then self destruct it.

## Proof of Concept
The initialize function of `ChakraSettlement.sol` calls the `public` `_Settlement_init(...)` function. The issue is that the `_Settlement_init(...)` function is `public` instead of `internal`. This allows anyone to be able to reset all the variables set in the initialize function by directly calling the `public` `_Settlement_init(...)` function. 

This way, an attacker can reset their address as the `owner` then call the `UUPSUpgradeable.upgradeToAndCall` function to upgrade to a malicious contract then self destruct it.

