The impact is high as the adversary can call the `receive_cross_chain_msg` with the already processed and valid parameters and benefit from it. With such parameters, anyone can call not just the validators so it further affects the protocol. Due to the missing check if the `txId` status is `UNKNOW` the attack is very much feasible as shown in the below fork testing local POC. This also breaks the main invariant mentioned in the contest docs/readme that 
